  "summary": "Australian Senator Skye Kakoschke-Moore from the Nick Xenophon Team announced her resignation after discovering she held dual British citizenship through her mother. Her mother, born in Singapore in 1957 when it was a British colony, had acquired British citizenship under the 1983 British Nationality Act, which Kakoschke-Moore inherited by descent when she was born in Darwin in 1985. She expressed being heartbroken by this discovery, as she had previously believed she was not British based on advice her father received from the British embassy when she was 12. The matter will be referred to the high court to determine how the Senate vacancy will be filled, with a recount likely to elect NXT candidate Tim Storrer. Nick Xenophon described the situation as uncharted legal territory and expressed devastation at losing Kakoschke-Moore, though he predicted it wouldn't be the end of her political career. Kakoschke-Moore stated her intention to continue with the NXT and potentially return to the Senate."
}
```

